      "body": "## Purpose\n\nFixes #60845.\n\nWith `--fully-sharded-loras`, the shared experts' LoRA layers all-gather / all-reduce across TP, and the routed experts' fused MoE LoRA kernel does its own collectives on the main stream. Running the shared experts on the aux stream puts two collectives in flight on the same communicator. Under CUDA graph capture they become independent graph branches, and the replay order is not guaranteed to match across ranks, so NCCL deadlocks (first LoRA decode step hangs, then `RPC call to sample_tokens timed out`).\n\nThis PR runs the shared experts on the main stream when fully-sharded LoRA is enabled, same as the existing EPLB / flashinfer exclusions in `SharedExperts._disable_shared_experts_overlap`.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nQwen3.5-35B-A3B, TP=2, `--enable-lora --fully-sharded-loras --max-lora-rank 32`, default CUDA graphs, two rank-32 adapters alternating.\n\n- v0.28.0 (reproduces the hang on the first LoRA request): with this patch, first request returns in 1s, 1000/1000 requests OK.\n- v0.31.0 / main: 1000/1000 requests OK.\n\n## Test Result\n\nNo hang, 0 failed in both runs.\n\n",
