      "body": "## Claude Code Review\n\nThis pull request is from a fork — automated review is disabled. A repository maintainer can comment `@claude review` to run a one-time review.",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/61284#pullrequestreview-5496532443",
      "id": 5496532443,
      "state": "COMMENTED",
      "submitted_at": "2026-10-12T22:18:14Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "claude[bot]"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "LGTM. The fix removes the concurrency instead of relying on enqueue order, and it matches the existing rule that LoRA's own dual stream is already disabled with `fully_sharded_loras` (`_build_lora_context`, `LoRAConfig` validation).\n\nValidated on 2× H20 (TP=2, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, 2D + 3D adapters, default CUDA graphs): v0.28.0 hangs on the first LoRA request (`RPC call to sample_tokens timed out`) and passes with `VLLM_DISABLE_SHARED_EXPERTS_STREAM=1`. Current main does not hang on H20 (same as B200), so whether it triggers really depends on the hardware. This PR passes, and its outputs differ from main only by the usual run-to-run noise.",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/61284#pullrequestreview-5560493636",
      "id": 5560493636,
      "state": "COMMENTED",
      "submitted_at": "2026-10-17T22:53:11Z",
